# Orrery — Controls

This file defines how a player operates the game: the pointer that places and
drags on the field, the keyboard actions everything else runs on, and the
focus rule that routes the editing keys. What each verb does in the editor is
in `specs/editor.md`, and the menus and screens the navigation actions drive
are in `specs/ui.md`. Every figure below carries the name this specification
gives it.

## The pointer

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
This game stands on no engine, so the pointer belongs to the runtime layer you
write. What the game reads from that layer is a pointer position in the game's
logical units on the `STAGE_W x STAGE_H` (`1280 x 720`) stage, a press edge,
and a release edge. How the layer produces those three is yours to decide.
{{else}}
The pointer belongs to the engine, which documents it in the `engine/`
directory at the root of this repository. What the game reads from it is a
pointer position in the game's logical units on the `STAGE_W x STAGE_H`
(`1280 x 720`) stage, a press edge, and a release edge.
{{/if}}

The game acts on those three alone. Each pointer position is resolved on its
own, in the order the positions arrive, so a drag's ghost and a track being
laid follow the pointer hex by hex. What a press, a move, and a release do in
each region of the editor is defined in `specs/editor.md`; hexes are targeted
by the rule in `specs/field.md`, and tray slots and tape cells by the
rectangles `specs/editor.md` fixes. The pointer operates the editor alone,
and never a menu.

## Focus

`state.editor.focus` is `field` or `tape`, and it routes the editing keys. A
press inside the tape panel's extent, `x >= 224` and `y >= TAPE_Y0` (`560`),
sets focus to `tape`; a press anywhere else on the editor screen sets it to
`field`. Focus is `field` on entering the editor.

Two focus-routed actions may share a physical key. Each action below is
registered on its own, the game reads the ones the current focus names, and a
press of a shared key is therefore unambiguous.

## Actions and bindings

`ACTIONS` holds every action the game registers, and `BINDINGS` maps each to
the `KeyboardEvent.code` values that fire it. Each action is read as a press
edge unless noted. The navigation and global actions apply as the screen
dictates; the field and tape actions apply on the editor screen under their
focus, and only while no run is active, except as `specs/editor.md` states.

### Navigation

| Action | Keys | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `up` | `ArrowUp` | Menus and select lists: moves the highlight up. Tape focus: selects the previous arm's row. |
| `down` | `ArrowDown` | The same, down, and the next arm's row. |
| `left` | `ArrowLeft` | How-to: previous page. Tape focus: moves the cursor one cell left. |
| `right` | `ArrowRight` | The same, next page, and one cell right. |
| `confirm` | `Enter` | Accepts the highlighted item. |
| `back` | `Escape` | Leaves the current screen; during a run, stops it, as `specs/simulation.md` states. |

### Global

| Action | Keys | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `mute` | `KeyM` | Toggles sound, from any screen. |
| `play` | `Space` | Editor: starts the run, or toggles running and paused. |
| `step` | `KeyN` | Editor: steps the run one cycle, as `specs/editor.md` states. |
| `speed-down` | `Comma` | Editor, during a run: the previous `SPEEDS` step. |
| `speed-up` | `Period` | Editor, during a run: the next `SPEEDS` step. |
| `undo` | `KeyU` | Editor, while editing: reverts the latest edit, as `specs/editor.md` defines. |
| `redo` | `KeyI` | Editor, while editing: re-applies the latest undone edit. |

### Field focus

| Action | Keys | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `part-cw` | `KeyE` | Rotates the selected or dragged part one step clockwise. |
| `part-ccw` | `KeyQ` | The same, counterclockwise. |
| `part-grow` | `KeyW` | Lengthens the selected or dragged arm, to at most `ARM_MAX_LEN` (`3`). |
| `part-shrink` | `KeyS` | The same, shorter, to at least `ARM_MIN_LEN` (`1`). |
| `part-delete` | `KeyX` | Removes the selected part. |

### Tape focus

| Action | Keys | Writes at the cursor |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ins-rotate-ccw` | `KeyA` | `rotate-ccw` |
| `ins-rotate-cw` | `KeyD` | `rotate-cw` |
| `ins-extend` | `KeyW` | `extend` |
| `ins-retract` | `KeyS` | `retract` |
| `ins-pivot-ccw` | `KeyZ` | `pivot-ccw` |
| `ins-pivot-cw` | `KeyC` | `pivot-cw` |
| `ins-grab` | `KeyG` | `grab` |
| `ins-drop` | `KeyV` | `drop` |
| `ins-advance` | `KeyT` | `advance` |
| `ins-recede` | `KeyB` | `recede` |
| `ins-blank` | `Delete` | A blank, without moving the cursor. |
| `ins-erase` | `Backspace` | Nothing: blanks the cell before the cursor and moves the cursor back one. |
| `ins-reset` | `KeyR` | The `reset` macro of `specs/instructions.md`. |
| `ins-repeat` | `KeyY` | The `repeat` macro of `specs/instructions.md`. |

How writing at the cursor advances it, and how the tape panel scrolls to keep
the cursor visible, are in `specs/editor.md`.
